flowchart TB
    accTitle: Evidence admission for a mechanism comparison
    accDescr: A candidate record is inspected for documented state and a trigger, control, or transition relationship. The comparison then tests node correspondence, edge correspondence, and a preserved invariant while recording what is missing. Shared nouns or similar outputs without control correspondence are insufficient.

    A[Candidate record]
    A --> B{Documented state?}
    B -->|No| X[Do not admit as a mechanism claim]
    B -->|Yes| C{Trigger and control or transition edge?}
    C -->|No| X
    C -->|Yes| D[Reconstruct the mechanism]
    D --> E{Node and edge correspondence?}
    E -->|No| X
    E -->|Yes| F{At least one preserved invariant?}
    F -->|No| X
    F -->|Yes| G[Admit a bounded comparison claim]
    G --> H[Record missing invariants and evidence limits]

    classDef source fill:#EAF4FB,stroke:#1A4A8A,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.3px;
    classDef decision fill:#F4F4F4,stroke:#888888,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef reject fill:#FEF9E7,stroke:#F39C12,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.1px;
    classDef accept fill:#EEF7EE,stroke:#27AE60,color:#1C1C1E,stroke-width:1.3px;
    class A,D source;
    class B,C,E,F decision;
    class X reject;
    class G,H accept;
